(Bug #75, the deeper shapes. A function that passes its own collection
 parameter on to another function, and one that passes it to itself, hold
 the pointer one frame further from the variable that owns it. The store-back
 has to travel the whole chain, not just the last hop, or growth stops one
 call short of home.)

To 'inner add' with a list called items.
    append "x" to items.

To 'outer add' with a list called items.
    'inner add' of items.

To 'three deep' with a list called items.
    'outer add' of items.

(Recursion: each frame's parameter is a link in the same chain.)
To 'fill' with a list called items and a number called left.
    If left is greater than 0,
        append "x" to items,
        'fill' of items and {left subtract 1}.

To 'store into' with a map called holder and a text called label.
    Set holder's "{label}" to 1.

To 'pass the map on' with a map called holder and a text called label.
    'store into' of holder and label.

a list called 'deep' is ["a"].
a number called n is 0.
While n is less than 20,
    'outer add' of 'deep',
    Set n to n add 1.
Print "two calls deep: {'deep''s length}".

a list called deeper is ["a"].
a number called d is 0.
While d is less than 20,
    'three deep' of deeper,
    Set d to d add 1.
Print "three calls deep: {deeper's length}".

a list called recursed is ["a"].
'fill' of recursed and 20.
Print "recursed: {recursed's length}".
Print "recursed last: {recursed's last}".

a map called m is {"seed": 0}.
a number called k is 0.
While k is less than 20,
    'pass the map on' of m and "k{k}",
    Set k to k add 1.
Print "a map, two calls deep: {m's length}".
